WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.860
Now, it is a different matter,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:12.420
what if this area has remained in that state for a very long, prolonged period of time,

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:18.500
and with age—I repeat, with age—

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:26.060
why does this kind of immobility and wooden stiffness begin to appear in the body?

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:34.440
Because calcium salts begin to settle and deposit right onto these fibrotic areas,

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:42.340
that is, this very fibrotic area—this somatic dysfunction, this restriction—

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.600
it begins to become coated with calcium salts.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.460
Calcification of the tissues takes place right in that spot.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.420
Even in medicine, this condition is called calcinosis or sclerosis,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.460
it is a stage of somatic dysfunction,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.720
it responds very poorly to correction,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.860
and is practically considered irreversible.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:22.200
Whereas fibrosis is still a reversible stage,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:33.380
of unwinding the fascia, sclerosis is a very difficult, very stubborn spot to work with.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:45.960
With fibro-sclerotic areas—that is, there is fibrosis and it is not calcified everywhere,

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:55.380
only in a few spots—you can still work with it somehow. When complete calcification of the area has occurred,

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:59.120
it has turned into pure stone—how can I put it—

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.840
marble, granite.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:08.820
And that is why there are so many elderly people whose spine has been twisted and bent,

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:14.660
because there are so many fascial ligaments there—the entire spine is literally wrapped in them:

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.660
spinous, transverse, longitudinal, spinous, transverse, oblique ligaments.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:25.100
That is, there is a huge number of ligaments in the spine,

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:34.560
and if fibrosis develops on some of these ligaments, and then gets coated with calcium salts,

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:42.480
then it turns out it can simply lock the spine in a certain fixed position,

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:49.620
that is, in a curve. And mostly it is this forward curve, because we sit all the time,

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.700
and older people work in the garden, constantly bent over.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:03:02.320
In our neighborhood, I saw one woman walking with a cane—she can barely walk anymore,

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:06.120
because her spine is literally bent over like this,

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.000
and her nose is literally down near her knees.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.300
And yet with her cane, somehow her joints still manage to work.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:22.000
That is sclerosis in its purest form—sclerosis of the ligaments of the spinal column.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.480
Or vascular sclerosis, which you already know about as well.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:34.980
That is, sclerosis is the spot where a plaque has formed on a blood vessel,

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:40.080
and then it began to calcify, that is, to harden with lime deposits,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.620
and naturally the vessel lost its ability to expand and contract,

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.740
and to flex along with the body.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:54.640
So vascular sclerosis is a very dangerous condition.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:59.960
Normal blood flow through the vessel is completely lost.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.320
How do we work with sclerosis?

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.500
We only release the surrounding tissues.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:15.360
That is, we palpate this fulcrum—we feel this calcified stone under our hands.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:22.700
You work with it, try to dissociate and free it somehow, watch where it is pulling and twisting.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:30.960
It twists the tissues, it keeps twisting the tissues, yet the stone itself does not respond to any osteopathic techniques.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:38.360
So this is not a very good stage—therefore, the earlier we start working on ourselves,

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:46.940
the lower our probability of developing sclerosis in any of our tissues.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:54.620
Remember: sclerosis is the deposition of calcium salts in places

00:04:54.680 --> 00:05:00.100
where calcium does not belong—that is, in soft tissues.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:08.640
Well, essentially, I have now told you the entire process of how a somatic dysfunction forms.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.480
It seems the body does all of this by itself.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.560
All of this happens automatically.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:21.940
And yet it turns out these are the kinds of problems that get created.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:30.820
As one very famous osteopath used to say: wait, shouldn't there be some kind of natural self-resorption?

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:41.060
Prolonged stress acting on this very system—that is, some kind of long-lasting impact.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:46.720
To explain it more simply to you—take the same thing, our everyday gadgets.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:52.440
If we constantly stay in that posture from morning until evening,

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.840
and sleep on our side with our knees pulled up,

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:00.580
how could adhesions NOT develop in the intestines?

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.060
How could problems with constipation NOT begin?

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:13.200
I don't know, that is the very least that can happen: gastritis, some kind of pleurisy in the lungs,

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:20.100
because here we compress them—or diseases of the peritoneum,

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:28.620
all sorts of pancreatitis. That is, everything ending in '-itis' has been named a disease in medicine,

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:32.120
because inflammations all end in '-itis'.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.340
That is why we have bronchitis, sinusitis,

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.400
I don't know,

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.640
pleurisy there,

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.060
gastritis, adnexitis,

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:44.660
what else do we have.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.200
That is, all of these are inflammatory reactions—the body creates all of this itself,

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:58.800
putting it up as protection. And as a result of the healing process, fibrotic plaques form.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:10.960
That is, the body sometimes places one there and simply forgets about it, forgets it even exists.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:20.420
Or it adapts to how a person finds it comfortable to sit in that posture, or comfortable to hate someone for years.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:25.320
Those are psychosomatic tensions—tissue will keep pulling into that area more and more,

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.260
until dysfunction of some organ or some system sets in.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:34.520
So it is very important to practice self-regulation.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:41.920
And our upcoming lessons will already be directly connected with practical techniques.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:46.240
I will explain the techniques. These are important lessons.
